<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <RootNamespace>Vixen.Gameplay.Shooting</RootNamespace>
        <Description>
            The weapon model and the hit claim's validation rules: hitscan and projectiles, spread and
            recoil patterns both ends compute identically, ammunition and reload, penetration and
            falloff — and the rewind budget, because a claim that costs a physics rewind must not cost
            a rate limiter the same as an ordinary call.
        </Description>
        <PackageTags>gameplay;shooting;weapons;fps;lag-compensation;game-engine;vixen</PackageTags>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" Visible="false" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!--
            ⚠ Shooting → Combat is a horizontal edge doc 28 § The dependency spine does not list, and
            it is added deliberately rather than by accident. What a weapon needs from Combat is the
            *damage pipeline* — a headshot is a Crit-stage rule, armour is a Mitigate one, and a game
            that had to reimplement those for bullets would have two sets of tested edge cases. The
            two are one milestone (G2) so nothing takes one without the other being available, and the
            trimmer removes the casting and threat machinery a pure shooter never calls.

            What it does *not* take is Vixen.Net. The hit path is doc 16's — prediction, the claim
            RPC, ColliderRollback — and none of it is new; what is new is the weapon model and the
            claim's validation rules, which are arithmetic over numbers the caller supplies.
        -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Vixen.Gameplay\Vixen.Gameplay.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Vixen.Gameplay.Combat\Vixen.Gameplay.Combat.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core\Vixen.Core.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Serialization\Vixen.Core.Serialization.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Reflection\Vixen.Core.Reflection.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Serialization.Generator\Vixen.Core.Serialization.Generator.csproj"
                          OutputItemType="Analyzer"
                          ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" />

        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Reflection.Generator\Vixen.Core.Reflection.Generator.csproj"
                          OutputItemType="Analyzer"
                          ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Vixen.Gameplay.Shooting.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
